description: Core App Router + layer conventions (slim)
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Core

- App Router only. Routes orchestrate; keep `page`/`layout` thin.
- Placement: route → `app/<route>/_components/<name>/index.tsx`; home/layout → `app/_components/<name>/index.tsx`; shared ≥2 routes → `components/<name>/index.tsx` (`ui/` flat).
- Reuse before redesign: existing shared/UI/`_components` first — extend with props; do not rebuild chrome per page (see `components.mdc`).
- Folder-per-component: `<name>/index.tsx` — never `_components/foo.tsx`.
- `lib/` = env/helpers/date; `db/` = database; `features/` = feature modules; `providers/` / `hooks/` / `types/` as needed.
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for interactivity.
- Direction: `useDirection()` from `@/hooks/use-direction` — do not set `dir` ad hoc on random nodes. Use logical CSS properties (`margin-inline`, `padding-inline`).
- Named exports `function Name()`; default exports only for Next route files.
- One `<main>` in root layout only.
- Database migrations: strictly backward-compatible with Dexie versioning (`.version(n).stores(...).upgrade(...)`). Never drop or wipe user data; offline IndexedDB records must seamlessly persist across app updates.
- If you change these conventions, update this rule + `AGENTS.md` together.
